From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:12:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] debian: do not restart ceph-mgr from manager module postinst
 scripts

Since ceph-mgr-modules-core got split into per-module packages, every
manager module package restarts a running ceph-mgr when it gets
configured. An upgrade from Tentacle installs about twenty of these
packages, and every later upgrade configures them again, so a single
apt run restarts the manager about twenty times in a row.

ceph-mgr@.service allows only three starts within 30 minutes. Once
that limit is hit, systemd leaves the unit failed with start-limit-hit
and does not restart it anymore. As try-restart still returns success,
the upgrade finishes without any error while the manager stays down
until 'systemctl reset-failed' is run. This also holds for the
dashboard, cephadm, diskprediction-local and rook packages, which
restarted the manager already before the split; installed together,
they exceed the limit on their own.

Restarting from postinst also starts the new manager version in the
middle of the package upgrade, before the monitors got restarted in the
recommended order. All other Ceph daemons are deliberately not
restarted on upgrade, see the dh_installsystemd options in
debian/rules.

Drop these postinst scripts, as restarting the manager was their only
purpose. After installing a manager module package on a node with a
running manager, restart the manager to load the new module.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
